cademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040289/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37358" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1024 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1024\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040289/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bf283bc2cfddc5d9a25b353c7ac44319704195febc4ff79f0c64c7bb355b8ba" "basis" 1427 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040289/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-86694" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the eigenvectors of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $T$ given that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]T=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040289/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bf283bc2cfddc5d9a25b353c7ac44319704195febc4ff79f0c64c7bb355b8ba" "basis" 1427 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040289/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-86694" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the matrix $[\\begin{aligned}7 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ appears on both sides of the equation. Since this matrix is invertible (its determinant is not zero), left-multiplying the equation by the inverse gives the following expression for $T:$\n\n$$\nT={{{[\\begin{aligned}7 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}}_{⏟}}_{P}{{[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{D}{{[\\begin{aligned}7 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{P}^{-1}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $T$ is diagonalizable. The eigenvalues of $T$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=5$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-4$ and the corresponding eigenvectors are the columns of the matrix $P.$ Computing $P,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P={[\\begin{aligned}7 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{-1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, the corresponding eigenvectors are: \n\n$\\,$ ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040289/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bf283bc2cfddc5d9a25b353c7ac44319704195febc4ff79f0c64c7bb355b8ba" "basis" 1427 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040289/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-86694" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040289/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "59e784e7d9e4e012a796856f8cab92078f7e25c11af7a1af50eeb1676151a3c7" "basis" 1427 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040289/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-86694" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040289/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bf283bc2cfddc5d9a25b353c7ac44319704195febc4ff79f0c64c7bb355b8ba" "basis" 1427 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040289/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-86694" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$[\\begin{aligned}-